{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795348096,"nonce":"jYxszXvCPqS6IX1FZgmo16VzC3s=","title":"Face-operator block coupled every DOF of the face-adjacent cells","message":"The face block's rows and columns were all DOFs of each facet's owner cell. For degree-2 N1E that is 20 per tet, of which only the 8 on the facet have a tangential trace there; the rest project to round-off. The stored block was several times larger than the face and the direct factorisation fill grew with it. On a periodic quartz|air cell with exact faces (degree 2, three meshes), the operator held 30 to 50 times the entries of the same cell with first-order faces.\n\nFix: keep only the rows and columns whose projection is above round-off of the block's largest (_nonzero_lines in _faceop_block). The operator entries drop about 6x, and the factorisation fill with them, and the field is unchanged to the printed digits (Fresnel check). Test: test_face_block_couples_only_the_face_dofs (red without the pruning).","files":null}]}